# WhatsApp templates must be documented before they can send

`apps/backend/docs/whatsapp-meta-templates.md` is the **submission checklist ops works from** in Meta Business Manager. A `templateKey` that exists only in code will never be approved, so every send using it fails silently at the WhatsApp channel.

## When to update the doc

Update it in the **same change** whenever you:

- Add a key to `TEMPLATE_NAMES` / `BODY_VARS` in `whatsapp-template.service.ts`
- Change a template's body variables, their **order**, or its CTA URL
- Rename or retire a Meta template

Reusing an already-listed template (e.g. sending `order_status_client` from a new flow) needs **no** doc change.

## What to add

1. A row in the table at the top: internal key, Meta name, category, body variables in positional order, button target.
2. A numbered section with `**Vars:**`, `**Button:**`, and the exact **en_US** and **fr** body copy, matching the format of the existing sections.

Keep the table row and the section consistent with `BODY_VARS` — the array order *is* the Meta `{{1}}, {{2}}, …` order.

## Meta body constraints

- Never start or end a body with a variable.
- Keep substantial fixed text around variables; short bodies with many variables get rejected.
- Category is **Utility** for all current templates.
- Dynamic URL buttons take the entity id only (`/app/orders/{{1}}`). A static CTA must send no button parameter.

## Prefer reuse over new templates

Each new template needs Meta review before it can send. If an approved template can carry the message (e.g. packing detail into `rs_order_status`'s `statusLabel` or `rs_admin_order_risk`'s `reason`), reuse it and say so in your summary rather than adding a key that blocks the feature on approval.
